{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/helperbuilds"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"How one helper source tree becomes two binaries, and how each feature finds out whether it can run.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacKit"}],"role":"article","title":"The App Store and Direct builds"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Headwire Helper ships in two builds from the same code:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The App Store build","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is sandboxed and has everything that needs no private API, input included. It is the default: a plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build"},{"text":" makes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Direct build","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is signed with Developer ID, notarized and unsandboxed. It adds only the code compiled under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HEADWIRE_PRIVATE_API"},{"text":": the virtual display that extends the Mac onto the device or gives a Mac with no display one, Apple’s Sidecar started from the menu, and answering the Mac’s side of Bluetooth pairing without a system dialog. Each of these is checked at run time and turns off rather than crashes when macOS has changed it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper input is compiled under a second switch, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HEADWIRE_HELPER_INPUT"},{"type":"text","text":", which is on by default in both builds and is turned off only should App Review refuse event posting. A build without it keeps streaming and shows input as unavailable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This documentation is generated from the App Store build, so the Direct build’s private-API types do not appear in it."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Which-build-is-running","text":"Which build is running"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/current"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the two compile-time switches and reports the build’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/Distribution-swift.enum"},{"type":"text","text":" and whether helper input is compiled in. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/launchLine(version:dryRun:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the first line the helper logs at launch."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Whether-a-feature-runs","text":"Whether a feature runs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperFeatures\/resolve(_:grants:build:)"},{"type":"text","text":" combines three inputs into one "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState"},{"type":"text","text":" for each feature:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The menu’s switch for it, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperToggles"},{"text":". Every switch starts off: the helper is optional, and streaming, input and extending the Mac begin only when the person turns them on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What macOS has granted, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/PermissionGrants"},{"text":". A switch that is on without its permission is ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needs(_:)"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Onboarding"},{"text":" walks the person through that one permission.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What the build contains. A feature the build lacks is ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/unavailable(_:)"},{"text":" with an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability"},{"text":" whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability\/menuText"},{"text":" is shown on the greyed-out control.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The extended display also needs streaming, so with its switch on and streaming not running it is "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needsStreaming"},{"type":"text","text":". The features go to the device as the helper’s capabilities, so the device greys out the same controls with the same reasons."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuilds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit"]]},"references":{"doc://HeadwireMacKit/documentation/HeadwireMacKit/He